ideo cards arranged in a partial carousel style with visible left and right overflow indicators. Below this, a grid-like arrangement for the 'My feed' videos with uniform thumbnail cards in rows of four or five, with equal spacing and margins. The 'Categories' section at the bottom uses a horizontally scrolling carousel grid of category tiles with consistent card sizes and spacing. The footer sits below these with minimal textual links aligned right. Padding throughout is generous, with vertical spacing between sections averaging 30-40 px, horizontal padding in content areas about 20-30 px. Text and elements use left alignment with center alignment only for search field input and navigation icons. Keywords for layout: two-column, vertical sidebar, horizontal top bar, horizontal scroll, grid cards, carousel, fixed sidebar, padded content area, consistent margins.\n- **Functions**: Users can perform specific actions like searching for videos, folders, or content using the search field; initiating video uploads from local computer or cloud storage; recording new videos from screen or webcam; creating new videos from templates; or hosting live events/webinars via dedicated buttons. The interface visually supports these actions with clear, icon-labeled call-to-action cards that invite interaction. Users can also browse their recent videos, adding new ones easily by clicking the 'New video' card. The video cards in the 'Recent videos' and 'My feed' sections allow users to interact via comments, privacy settings, viewing stats, and sharing links, supporting content management and engagement workflows. Medium-level tasks include organizing and managing video content, exploring recommended or curated feeds like 'Vimeo Staff Picks', and browsing content categories for discovery. This facilitates efficient content curation and consumption by the user. The broader goal enabled by this interface is to allow users to manage their video content library, upload or create new conten